{"type":"standard","title":"Dhatki language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Dhatki language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q32480","titles":{"canonical":"Dhatki_language","normalized":"Dhatki language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Dhatki language</span></span>"},"pageid":3023140,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Dhatki_language.png/330px-Dhatki_language.png","width":330,"height":273},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/Dhatki_language.png","width":362,"height":299},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1354020056","tid":"140f24e4-4f0a-11f1-a6c2-ef3187c0abb3","timestamp":"2026-05-13T20:26:53Z","description":"Indo-Aryan language of India","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhatki_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhatki_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhatki_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dhatki_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhatki_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Dhatki_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhatki_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dhatki_language"}},"extract":"Dhatki, also known as Dhatti, Thari, is a Indo-Aryan language of the Indo-European language family. It is mainly spoken in Tharparkar and Umerkot districts of Sindh, and in the Barmer and Jaisalmer districts of Rajasthan.","extract_html":"<p><b>Dhatki</b>, also known as <b>Dhatti</b>, <b>Thari</b>, is a Indo-Aryan language of the Indo-European language family. It is mainly spoken in Tharparkar and Umerkot districts of Sindh, and in the Barmer and Jaisalmer districts of Rajasthan.</p>"}